<title>BELGIUM: Sabena says pilots' strike over.</title>
<headline>Sabena says pilots' strike over.</headline>
<dateline>BRUSSELS 1996-10-31</dateline>
<text>
<p>Belgian airline Sabena said on Thursday that a strike by pilots had ended at 2:30 p.m. (1330 GMT) and that flights were now leaving on time again.</p>
<p>&quot;The operation is normal again,&quot; a spokesman said. &quot;By going back to work the pilots are signalling they are more open to discussions with management,&quot; he added.</p>
<p>The pilots went on strike on Thursday to protest against a draft deal between Sabena management and trade unions on a $4.7 billion Belgian francs ($151 million) profitability plan.</p>
<p>Sabena earlier said 25 of its 70 flights had been cancelled. Other flights had faced delays of up to an hour.</p>
